1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:03,420
( knocking on door )

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,672
HEY.
HI. MY NAME'S
CHANDLER.

3
00:00:04,672 --> 00:00:06,548
I JUST MOVED
IN NEXT DOOR

4
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:08,634
AND I WAS WONDERING IF YOU'D
BE INTERESTED IN BATTLING ME

5
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:10,636
IN A POST-APOCALYPTIC
WORLD FOR CONTROL

6
00:00:10,636 --> 00:00:14,389
OF THE GALAXY'S LAST
REMAINING ENERGY SOURCE?

7
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:15,557
SURE, NEIGHBOR.

8
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:17,935
COME ON IN.

9
00:00:17,935 --> 00:00:19,102
SO, IS JANINE AROUND?

10
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:20,646
UH, NO, SHE'S AT DANCE CLASS.

11
00:00:20,646 --> 00:00:22,230
CAN I SEE
WHAT SHE DID WITH MY ROOM?

12
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,065
YEAH, BUT, HEY,
DON'T GO THROUGH HER STUFF.

13
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,275
SHE GETS REALLY MAD.

14
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:29,905
OH, MY GOD.

15
00:00:29,905 --> 00:00:31,782
WHAT IS THI...

16
00:00:31,782 --> 00:00:33,701
IT'S LIKE A GUY NEVER LIVED
IN HERE.

17
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:35,285
LOOK, YOU GOT TO BE CAREFUL.

18
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:36,912
THIS GIRL THING IS DANGEROUS.

19
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:38,205
IT'S SPREADING ALREADY.

20
00:00:38,205 --> 00:00:39,915
IT IS?

21
00:00:39,915 --> 00:00:42,501
YES, IS THIS
YOUR PRETTY PINK PILLOW

22
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:43,919
ON THE COUCH?

23
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,128
NO.

24
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,797
IS THAT YOUR
TINY LITTLE BOX

25
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:48,966
THAT'S TOO SMALL
TO PUT ANYTHING IN?

26
00:00:48,966 --> 00:00:49,967
NO.

27
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,927
NO. OKAY, THIS IS NOT GOOD.

28
00:00:51,927 --> 00:00:53,804
YOU ARE A GUY, OKAY?

29
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:55,597
THIS IS A
GUY'S PLACE.

30
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,224
IF YOU LET THIS GO,
YOU'LL BE SITTING AROUND

31
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:59,935
WITH YOUR FINGERS
SOAKING IN STUFF.

32
00:00:59,935 --> 00:01:01,269
ALL RIGHT,
YOU'RE RIGHT.

33
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:02,479
I'LL-I'LL-I'LL TALK
TO HER.

34
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:03,689
YES, TALK TO HER--
BE A MAN.

35
00:01:03,689 --> 00:01:04,899
I'M A MAN.
DEFEND YOURSELF.

36
00:01:04,899 --> 00:01:06,149
( grunts )

37
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,776
CHANDLER,
COME ON.

38
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,444
WE HAVE TO HEM
THE NEW DUST RUFFLE.

39
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:11,613
BE RIGHT THERE,
SWEETUMS.

40
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:13,281
OKAY.

41
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:15,200
A TOTALLY DIFFERENT
SITUATION.

42
00:01:22,541 --> 00:01:28,047
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

43
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:30,257
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

44
00:01:30,257 --> 00:01:32,551
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

45
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:37,556
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

46
00:01:37,556 --> 00:01:39,767
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

47
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:43,102
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

48
00:01:43,102 --> 00:01:46,314
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

49
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:52,153
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

50
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:57,952
HEY, GUYS.

51
00:01:57,952 --> 00:02:00,287
HEY, HOW WAS YOUR BREAKFAST
WITH HILLARY?
IT WAS OKAY.

52
00:02:00,287 --> 00:02:01,705
SHE'S STILL KINDA DEPRESSED

53
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:03,874
BECAUSE SHE BROKE UP
WITH HER BOYFRIEND.

54
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:07,252
WELL, IS THIS HILLARY
YOUR HOT ASSISTANT CHEF HILLARY?

55
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:08,253
YEAH.

56
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:09,463
THE ONE THAT ALWAYS STARES AT ME

57
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:11,214
WHEN I COME IN?

58
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:13,341
NO, THE ONE WHO
LOOKED AT YOU ONCE

59
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:15,218
BECAUSE YOU
GOT IN HER WAY.

60
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:18,555
STILL, I COULD TELL SHE WAS
INTO ME.

61
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:22,101
WELL, WHY DON'T YOU SET US UP?

62
00:02:22,101 --> 00:02:24,061
OOH, ARE YOU SETTING ROSS UP
WITH SOMEONE?

63
00:02:24,061 --> 00:02:26,647
DOES SHE HAVE A WEDDING DRESS?

64
00:02:28,649 --> 00:02:29,650
HEY.
HEY.

65
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:31,026
RACHEL?
YEAH?

66
00:02:31,026 --> 00:02:33,028
LISTEN, I'M, UM,
MAKING UP FLYERS

67
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:35,114
TRYING TO GET
NEW MASSAGE CLIENTS.

68
00:02:35,114 --> 00:02:37,908
SO, CAN I COME TO BLOOMINGDALE'S
AND USE THE COPY MACHINE?

69
00:02:37,908 --> 00:02:40,410
WELL, SURE, BUT THEY MIGHT
THINK IT'S KIND OF WEIRD

70
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,746
CONSIDERING I DON'T
WORK THERE ANYMORE.

71
00:02:42,746 --> 00:02:43,872
OH, MY GOD!

72
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:45,540
WHAT HAPPENED?

73
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,626
I-I GOT A JOB
AT RALPH LAUREN.

74
00:02:47,626 --> 00:02:48,794
WELL, THAT'S GREAT!

75
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:50,295
CONGRATULATIONS!

76
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:52,213
WOW!

77
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:54,257
( chuckling ):
A YEAR AGO.

78
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:56,677
YOU'VE LASTED
A WHOLE YEAR.

79
00:02:56,677 --> 00:02:57,886
GOOD FOR YOU.

80
00:02:57,886 --> 00:02:58,887
OH.

81
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:00,347
( chuckles )

82
00:03:00,347 --> 00:03:02,141
BUT, PHEEBS,
YOU-YOU CAN STILL USE

83
00:03:02,141 --> 00:03:03,767
THE COPY MACHINE
WHERE I ACTUALLY WORK.

84
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:05,102
BUT JUST COME
BY AT LUNCH

85
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:06,311
SO THAT MY BOSS
DOESN'T SEE YOU

86
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:07,855
'CAUSE KIM WILL
JUST FREAK OUT

87
00:03:07,855 --> 00:03:09,606
AND SHE ALREADY DOESN'T
LIKE ME VERY MUCH.

88
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:11,441
I DON'T THINK MY BOSS
LIKES ME, EITHER.

89
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:13,192
I DON'T THINK MINE
LIKES ME, EITHER.

90
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:16,279
MAYBE IT'S A UNIVERSAL THING.

91
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:18,949
OR MAYBE... IT'S
BECAUSE YOU'RE ALL
HANGING AROUND HERE

92
00:03:18,949 --> 00:03:20,117
AT 11:30
ON A WEDNESDAY.

93
00:03:23,078 --> 00:03:25,580
YEAH, LET'S HEAD
OFF TO WORK.
WE SHOULD GO.

94
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:31,252
THANK YOU.

95
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:32,295
SURE.

96
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,173
NOW, YOU WILL NOT
BELIEVE THIS

97
00:03:34,173 --> 00:03:36,091
BUT I WAS IN THE COPY ROOM,
MAKING COPIES

98
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:37,300
AND RALPH LAUREN CAME IN.

99
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,301
OH, MY GOD.

100
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:39,511
DID YOU TALK TO HIM?

101
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:40,512
YEAH, A LITTLE.

102
00:03:40,512 --> 00:03:41,805
HE SEEMS REALLY NICE.

103
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:42,890
GOOD KISSER.

104
00:03:42,890 --> 00:03:44,058
WHAT?

105
00:03:44,058 --> 00:03:45,184
WHAT?

106
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:47,978
YOU KISSED HIM?
TOTALLY.

107
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:48,979
( gasps )

108
00:03:48,979 --> 00:03:50,647
PHOEBE, ARE YOU SERIOUS?

109
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:52,066
YEAH. I WAS JUST IN THERE.

110
00:03:52,066 --> 00:03:53,441
HE CAME IN,
HE INTRODUCED HIMSELF

111
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:54,568
AND, THEN, NEXT THING I KNOW,

112
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:56,862
WE'RE MAKING OUT, YOU KNOW.

113
00:03:56,862 --> 00:04:00,115
PHOEBE, I MEAN,
YOU DO KNOW HE'S MARRIED?

114
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:03,284
NO.
PHOEBE...

115
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:05,620
WHAT AM I SUPPOSED TO DO--
ASK EVERY GUY I MAKE OUT WITH

116
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:08,540
IF HE'S MARRIED?

117
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,917
NO, YEAH, I SHOULD, I SHOULD.

118
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:23,346
HEY, JOEY.

119
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:24,389
HEY.

120
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:25,515
UH, CAN I
TALK TO YOU

121
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:26,558
FOR A SECOND?

122
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:28,143
THIS, UH, KID
IN THIS PICTURE.

123
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:29,436
DO YOU, UH, YOU KNOW THIS KID?

124
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:31,146
IS THAT LIKE A RELATIVE
OR SOMETHING?

125
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,272
NO, I JUST THOUGHT IT WAS CUTE.

126
00:04:33,272 --> 00:04:34,649
YEAH, THAT'S
WHAT I WAS AFRAID OF.

127
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:37,318
OKAY, UH...
LOOK, JANINE,

128
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:39,696
I REALLY WANT YOU
TO FEEL AT HOME HERE

129
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:42,824
BUT SOME OF THIS NEW STUFF,
IT'S JUST... IT'S TOO GIRLIE.

130
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:43,825
OH.

131
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:44,868
LIKE WHAT?

132
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:46,203
LIKE THIS--

133
00:04:46,203 --> 00:04:48,747
PICTURES OF CUTE BABIES
WE DON'T KNOW.

134
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:50,665
WE-WE CAN'T HAVE THAT.

135
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:52,209
JOEY, IT'S ANNE GEDDES.

136
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:53,668
SHE'S A FAMOUS ARTIST.

137
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,462
LOOK, I DON'T KNOW THIS BABY.

138
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:58,215
I DON'T KNOW
IF SHE'S A FAMOUS ARTIST OR NOT

139
00:04:58,215 --> 00:05:00,134
YOU KNOW, AND...

140
00:05:00,134 --> 00:05:01,760
I DON'T WANT TO BE A JERK

141
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:04,888
BUT YOU'RE-YOU'RE CHANGING
TOO MUCH AROUND HERE.

142
00:05:04,888 --> 00:05:06,389
WELL, I'M SORRY,
I JUST THOUGHT I'D TRY

143
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:08,349
AND MAKE THE PLACE
A LITTLE NICER.

144
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:10,144
YEAH, BUT IT'S-IT'S
TOO MUCH STUFF.

145
00:05:10,144 --> 00:05:11,561
YOU KNOW,
LIKE YOU GOT THE CANDLES

146
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:14,397
AND THE FOOFY
SCHMOOFER THING HERE

147
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,191
AND, THEN, OVER HERE

148
00:05:16,191 --> 00:05:19,069
YOU GOT A PICTURE
OF A WATERING CAN.

149
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:20,612
WELL, I JUST THOUGHT...

150
00:05:20,612 --> 00:05:23,115
I'M SURE IT'S
A FAMOUS WATERING CAN, OKAY,

151
00:05:23,115 --> 00:05:24,616
BUT, COME ON...

152
00:05:24,616 --> 00:05:26,785
AND WHAT IS
WITH THE REALLY HOT STICK

153
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:27,995
IN THE BATHROOM?

154
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:30,705
IT'S A CURLING IRON.

155
00:05:36,044 --> 00:05:37,129
OH.

156
00:05:37,129 --> 00:05:39,214
WELL-WELL, THAT'S OKAY, THEN...

157
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:41,216
BUT, OKAY, MY TOWELS
FOR INSTANCE, OKAY.

158
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:42,843
I COME INTO
THE BATHROOM HERE

159
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:47,264
AND MY TOWEL IS NOT
ON THE FLOOR WHERE I KEEP IT.

160
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:49,850
IT'S UP HERE,
ON SOME HOOK

161
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:52,227
AND...
SMELLS DIFFERENT.

162
00:05:52,227 --> 00:05:53,603
IT'S CLEAN.

163
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:55,272
YEAH, WELL,
IT FEELS DIFFERENT.

164
00:05:55,272 --> 00:05:58,650
IT'S DRY.

165
00:05:58,650 --> 00:06:02,154
ALL RIGHT, I CAN MAKE MY PEACE
WITH THE CLEAN, DRY TOWELS...

166
00:06:02,154 --> 00:06:04,572
AND, OKAY, ALSO WHAT IS
WITH THESE CHIPS YOU BOUGHT?

167
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:06,658
NO, NO, NO.
IT'S POTPOURRI.

168
00:06:06,658 --> 00:06:08,493
YOU'RE SUPPOSED
TO SMELL IT.

169
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,753
( voice cracking ):
WELL, THAT'S LIKE SUMMER
IN A BOWL.

170
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:30,431
OH.

171
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:31,975
KIM, HI.

172
00:06:31,975 --> 00:06:33,810
UH-HUH.

173
00:06:35,062 --> 00:06:36,688
( clears throat )

174
00:06:36,688 --> 00:06:39,274
SO, YOU KNOW, I-I-I HANDED
IN THAT MARKETING REPORT

175
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:41,985
AND I... AND I NEVER GOT
TO HEAR WHAT YOU THOUGHT.

176
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:43,278
I DIDN'T READ IT.

177
00:06:43,278 --> 00:06:44,863
AH.

178
00:06:44,863 --> 00:06:46,614
( sighs )

179
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,242
SO, WOW, THE SPRING LINE--

180
00:06:48,242 --> 00:06:50,827
IT'S REALLY GOING TO BE
GREAT THIS YEAR, HUH?

181
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,411
YEAH.

182
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:56,917
( sighs )

183
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,127
SO, I HEAR, UH, RALPH
LAUREN FOOLED AROUND

184
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,754
WITH SOMEONE IN
THE COPY ROOM.

185
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:04,507
TELL ME EVERYTHING.

186
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:08,929
HEY, GUYS.

187
00:07:08,929 --> 00:07:10,055
HEY.

188
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:11,348
WHAT'S UP?

189
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:15,476
YOU KNOW...

190
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:17,979
OH, MY GOD.

191
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,981
WHAT HAPPENED
TO YOUR TEETH?

192
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,275
I WHITENED THEM.

193
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,945
REALLY?

194
00:07:24,945 --> 00:07:26,113
YEAH.

195
00:07:26,113 --> 00:07:28,156
WH-WHAT DO YOU THINK?

196
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:31,076
WELL, I THINK I SHOULDN'T LOOK
DIRECTLY AT THEM.

197
00:07:31,076 --> 00:07:33,036
COME ON, SERIOUSLY.

198
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:37,832
ROSS, THEY'RE REALLY,
REALLY, REALLY WHITE.

199
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:41,628
YEAH, WHAT WAS WRONG WITH
YOUR OLD... HUMAN TEETH?

200
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:46,174
OH, I-I DID LEAVE THE GEL ON
A LITTLE LONGER THAN IT SAID TO.

201
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:47,634
HOW MUCH LONGER?

202
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,428
A-A-A DAY.

203
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:53,056
ROSS, YOU KNOW THAT TONIGHT IS
YOUR DATE WITH HILLARY?

204
00:07:53,056 --> 00:07:54,766
I KNOW.
THAT'S WHY I DID IT.

205
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:57,894
COME ON,
ARE THEY REALLY THAT BAD?

206
00:07:57,894 --> 00:08:00,397
NO. NO, NO, NO,
YOU'LL-YOU'LL BE FINE.

207
00:08:00,397 --> 00:08:02,649
HILLARY'S BLIND, RIGHT?

208
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:04,318
SHE WILL BE
AFTER TONIGHT.

209
00:08:04,318 --> 00:08:05,777
YEAH.

210
00:08:07,528 --> 00:08:08,738
OH, HEY, HEY,
RACHE, UH

211
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,157
DO YOU NOTICE
ANYTHING...

212
00:08:10,157 --> 00:08:12,491
YEAH, YOUR TEETH?
YES, I SAW THEM FROM OUTSIDE.

213
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:17,247
YOU GUYS ARE NEVER
GOING TO BELIEVE THIS

214
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:19,791
BUT PHOEBE... MADE OUT...

215
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:21,584
WITH RALPH LAUREN.

216
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:23,086
WHAT?
OH, MY GOD.

217
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:24,754
YEAH, I KNOW.
SHE RAN INTO HIM AT MY OFFICE

218
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:27,090
AND THEY JUST... MADE OUT

219
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:29,301
AND THE CRAZIEST THING IS
NOW MY BOSS LIKES ME

220
00:08:29,301 --> 00:08:30,677
BECAUSE I TOLD HER ABOUT IT
AND SHE SAID IT WAS

221
00:08:30,677 --> 00:08:32,595
THE BEST GOSSIP
SHE'D HEARD ALL YEAR.

222
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:35,098
I AM PROUD OF ALL
MY FRIENDS TODAY.

223
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:37,184
MY GOD, RACHEL,
I CAN'T BELIEVE

224
00:08:37,184 --> 00:08:39,560
PHOEBE MADE OUT
WITH RALPH LAUREN.

225
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:42,105
OH, I'M SO JEALOUS.

226
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:45,608
HI, I'M CHANDLER,
YOUR LIVE-IN BOYFRIEND.

227
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:48,236
CHANDLER, PLEASE,
COME ON.

228
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:50,238
LOOK AT HIM.

229
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:54,784
OH, I AM NO WOMAN, BUT
THAT IS ONE TASTY DISH.

230
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:55,994
HEY.

231
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:57,496
HERE.

232
00:08:57,496 --> 00:09:00,665
OOH, WHO'S
THE SILVER FOX?

233
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:03,335
THAT-THAT IS
YOUR MAKE-OUT BUDDY.

234
00:09:03,335 --> 00:09:05,295
DON'T YOU RECOGNIZE HIM?

235
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:06,296
OH, WAIT.

236
00:09:06,296 --> 00:09:07,881
OOH, PHOEBE, I LOVE YOU.

237
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:10,425
KISS ME, PLEASE.

238
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:12,260
THAT'S NOT RALPH LAUREN.

239
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:14,304
SOUNDS LIKE HIM, THOUGH.

240
00:09:14,304 --> 00:09:15,763
WHAT?

241
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:17,307
YEAH, NO, RALPH'S...

242
00:09:17,307 --> 00:09:18,517
DOESN'T LOOK ANYTHING LIKE
THAT GUY.

243
00:09:18,517 --> 00:09:20,143
HE'S-HE'S YOUNG

244
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:23,397
AND HE'S GOT LONG HAIR
AND A BEARD AND A HACKY SACK.

245
00:09:23,397 --> 00:09:25,524
OH, MY GOD, PHOEBE,
THAT'S NOT RALPH LAUREN.

246
00:09:25,524 --> 00:09:27,734
THAT'S KENNY THE COPY GUY.

247
00:09:27,734 --> 00:09:29,819
WHAT?

248
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:32,239
OH, G... OH...
AND I TOLD MY BOSS

249
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:34,074
THAT SOMEONE MADE OUT
WITH RALPH LAUREN.

250
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:35,867
IF SHE FINDS OUT
THAT I LIED TO HER

251
00:09:35,867 --> 00:09:37,118
SHE IS GOING
TO HATE ME EVEN MORE.

252
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,161
PHOEBE!

253
00:09:38,161 --> 00:09:39,496
WHY WOULD THE COPY GUY

254
00:09:39,496 --> 00:09:40,997
SAY THAT HE'S RALPH LAUREN?

255
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,916
TO GET YOU TO MAKE OUT WITH HIM.

256
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:44,959
OH.

257
00:09:50,173 --> 00:09:51,341
OKAY, MAYBE
THIS WILL MAKE

258
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:54,135
YOUR TEETH LOOK
LESS WHITE.

259
00:09:57,222 --> 00:09:59,640
NOPE. NOPE.

260
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,309
OKAY, SO, UH, COLORS
THAT DON'T WORK ARE

261
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:03,520
BLUE, YELLOW,
GREEN, RED

262
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:06,981
BLACK, WHITE,
ORANGE AND PURPLE.

263
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:08,525
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT I'M GOING TO DO.

264
00:10:08,525 --> 00:10:11,403
THE DATE STARTS
IN, LIKE, AN HOUR.

265
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:14,072
HEY, ROSS, MAYBE IF
YOUR SKIN WAS LIGHTER

266
00:10:14,072 --> 00:10:16,450
YOUR TEETH WOULDN'T
LOOK SO BRIGHT.

267
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:17,742
OH, GREAT.

268
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,077
SO, I ALL NEED TO DO IS
GET SOME NEW SKIN.

269
00:10:19,077 --> 00:10:21,162
THANK YOU.

270
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:22,622
I'M JUST SAYING
IF WE PUT

271
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:24,583
JUST A LITTLE BIT
OF MAKEUP ON YOU...

272
00:10:24,583 --> 00:10:25,750
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA.

273
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:28,295
WE'RE NOT 13 ANYMORE.

274
00:10:29,921 --> 00:10:31,839
ROSS, THIS IS THE
ONLY THING LEFT

275
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,300
THAT HAS A SHOT
AT WORKING.

276
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:35,552
BUT WON'T SHE NOTICE
I HAVE MAKEUP ON?

277
00:10:35,552 --> 00:10:37,971
PLEASE, HALF THE GUYS
OUT THERE HAVE MAKEUP ON.

278
00:10:37,971 --> 00:10:40,014
WHAT?

279
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,391
ALL RIGHT,
HALF THE PEOPLE.

280
00:10:41,391 --> 00:10:43,393
I MEAN... WILL YOU
JUST TRY IT AND SEE?

281
00:10:43,393 --> 00:10:45,019
NO, I AM NOT
PUTTING ON MAKE-UP.

282
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:46,020
( knocking at door )

283
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,523
HELLO?
OH, GOOD.

284
00:10:48,523 --> 00:10:50,733
ROSS, COULD YOU PUT UP SOME
OF THESE FLYERS FOR ME?

285
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:53,236
NO! DEMON! DEMON!

286
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:01,119
NOW OUR DRAWERS
WILL SMELL NICE

287
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:04,581
AND WE DIDN'T WASTE
THESE PANTYHOSE.

288
00:11:04,581 --> 00:11:06,374
YES, GOD FORBID WE
THROW OUT OLD UNDERWEAR.

289
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:08,376
YOU KNOW WHAT?

290
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:10,837
I'M-I'M GOING TO... I'M
GOING TO GO OVER TO JOEY'S.

291
00:11:10,837 --> 00:11:13,089
WE'RE SUPPOSE TO ORGANIZE
THE WRAPPING-PAPER DRAWER.

292
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,675
YES, BUT I FEEL LIKE I'VE
REALLY GOTTEN IN TOUCH

293
00:11:16,675 --> 00:11:18,845
WITH MY FEMININE SIDE
ENOUGH TODAY, YOU KNOW.

294
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:20,263
IN FACT, I THINK
WE'RE TWO SACHETS

295
00:11:20,263 --> 00:11:21,764
AWAY FROM BECOMING
A LESBIAN COUPLE.

296
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:24,601
YOU KNOW WHAT?

297
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:25,684
THIS HAS BEEN
KIND OF A GIRLIE DAY.

298
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:26,853
YOU'RE RIGHT. I'M SORRY.

299
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:28,480
NAH, NAH,
THAT'S OKAY.

300
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,064
I-I FEEL LIKE I NEED
TO BE IN A GUY PLACE...

301
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:32,192
YOU KNOW, DO KIND OF,
LIKE, A MAN THING.

302
00:11:32,192 --> 00:11:33,734
YEAH. GO OVER TO JOEY'S.

303
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:35,736
GO OVER TO JOEY'S
AND-AND DRINK SOME BEER

304
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:37,947
AND HAMMER UP
SOME DRYWALL.

305
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:39,574
YOU KNOW, WHEN
GUYS HANG OUT

306
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:42,536
THEY DON'T JUST DRINK BEER
AND HAMMER UP DRYWALL.

307
00:11:42,536 --> 00:11:44,371
WHEN GIRLS HANG OUT,
WE DON'T HAVE PILLOW FIGHTS

308
00:11:44,371 --> 00:11:45,330
IN OUR UNDERWEAR.

309
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:49,042
I'M SORRY.

310
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:50,043
WE DO.

311
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:51,127
WE DO.

312
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:52,587
I DON'T KNOW
WHY I SAID THAT.

313
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:57,884
HEY, CHANDLER.

314
00:11:57,884 --> 00:11:59,386
COME ON IN.

315
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:01,929
WE'RE KNITTING
POT HOLDERS.

316
00:12:03,557 --> 00:12:05,766
NO THANKS, JOSEPHINE.

317
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:07,435
( door shuts )

318
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:11,064
HEY, ROSS, I WAS
WONDERING IF...

319
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:16,319
OH, MY GOD!

320
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:18,613
WHERE ARE ALL THE MEN?

321
00:12:18,613 --> 00:12:20,240
( door closes )

322
00:12:28,206 --> 00:12:29,999
OH, HI, KIM.

323
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:31,543
HI, RACHEL.

324
00:12:31,543 --> 00:12:33,294
REMEMBER THAT THING
I TOLD YOU

325
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:34,504
THAT HAPPENED YESTERDAY?

326
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,130
WELL, IT DIDN'T HAPPEN.

327
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:38,757
YOU DIDN'T CANCEL THE
FABRIC ORDER FROM TAIWAN?

328
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:40,635
OKAY, TWO THINGS
DIDN'T HAPPEN.

329
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:44,055
BUT, NO, REMEMBER I TOLD YOU
THAT SOMEONE MADE OUT WITH

330
00:12:44,055 --> 00:12:45,890
RALPH LAUREN
IN THE COPY ROOM?

331
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:47,766
WELL, IT TURNS OUT
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

332
00:12:47,766 --> 00:12:49,185
THAT'S NOT TRUE?

333
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:50,353
NO.
OH, THAT'S
INTERESTING

334
00:12:50,353 --> 00:12:52,021
BECAUSE I CHECKED.

335
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:53,523
AND ONLY ONE
KEY CARD WAS USED

336
00:12:53,523 --> 00:12:55,900
TO ACCESS THE COPY MACHINE
YESTERDAY DURING LUNCH

337
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,902
AND THAT KEY CARD
BELONGED TO YOU, RACHEL.

338
00:12:57,902 --> 00:12:59,112
OH, NO.
NO, NO, NO, NO.

339
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:01,239
OH, GOD, YOU THINK
I MADE OUT WITH HIM?

340
00:13:01,239 --> 00:13:02,490
LISTEN TO ME.

341
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:04,033
IF YOU THINK
SLEEPING WITH RALPH

342
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:06,578
IS GOING TO GET YOU MY JOB,
YOU ARE SADLY MISTAKEN.

343
00:13:06,578 --> 00:13:08,580
I DON'T WANT YOUR JOB.
I DON'T!

344
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:10,164
THIS IS SUCH A MISTAKE.

345
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:11,708
I DID NOT
MAKE OUT WITH HIM.

346
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:13,710
NOBODY MADE OUT WITH HIM.

347
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:15,920
I DID NOT USE
MY KEY CARD YESTERDAY.

348
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,797
I DON'T EVEN KNOW
HOW TO USE MY KEY CARD.

349
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:20,467
HI, RALPH.

350
00:13:20,467 --> 00:13:21,760
HI, KIM.

351
00:13:40,695 --> 00:13:42,781
YEAH, NOTHING HAPPENED.

352
00:13:42,781 --> 00:13:46,242
YOU COULD CUT THE
SEXUAL TENSION IN
HERE WITH A KNIFE.

353
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:55,502
AND AFTER THAT, WHAT COULD
I DO EXCEPT BECOME A CHEF.

354
00:13:55,502 --> 00:13:57,587
MM-HMM.

355
00:13:57,587 --> 00:14:00,006
AND SOMEDAY SOON, I HOPE
TO OPEN MY OWN RESTAURANT.

356
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:02,300
MMM.

357
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:04,969
YOU KNOW, YOU'RE A
REALLY GREAT LISTENER.

358
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:08,097
MOST GUYS I GO OUT WITH,
THEY JUST TALK AND TALK.

359
00:14:08,097 --> 00:14:11,267
MM-HMM.

360
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:13,770
AFTER A WHILE, IT'S
JUST, LIKE, SHUT YOUR
MOUTH, YOU KNOW?

361
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:16,606
( stifled chuckle):
HMM-HMM!

362
00:14:16,606 --> 00:14:18,149
I'VE PROBABLY BEEN
TALKING TOO MUCH.

363
00:14:18,149 --> 00:14:19,984
WHY DON'T WE TALK
ABOUT YOU A LITTLE BIT?

364
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:22,696
MM-MMM.

365
00:14:22,696 --> 00:14:24,322
COME ON, I
WANT TO KNOW.

366
00:14:24,322 --> 00:14:27,241
HMM-HMM-HMM.

367
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:28,827
OKAY.

368
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:31,162
I, UM, I'M FROM
LONG ISLAND.

369
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:33,748
I CAME TO THE CITY
FOR COLLEGE.

370
00:14:33,748 --> 00:14:36,917
UM, I, UH,
I HAVE A FIVE-YEAR-OLD SON.

371
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:38,670
AND IN MY SPARE TIME

372
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:40,839
I LIKE TO READ SPY NOVELS

373
00:14:40,839 --> 00:14:43,675
BUT LET'S TALK MORE
ABOUT YOU, HMM?

374
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:48,887
SO WHAT'S REALLY NEAT IS

375
00:14:48,887 --> 00:14:50,807
IF YOU SEAR THE STEMS
OF THE FLOWERS FIRST

376
00:14:50,807 --> 00:14:52,266
IN A FRYING PAN,

377
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:55,353
YOU'RE ARRANGEMENT
WILL LOOK FRESH MUCH LONGER.

378
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:58,231
OH, MY GOD, JOEY, THAT
IS SUCH A GREAT TIP.

379
00:14:58,231 --> 00:15:00,525
MONICA, CAN YOU EXCUSE US
FOR A SECOND?

380
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:03,069
I NEED TO TALK TO THE GIRL
WITH THE FLOWERS.

381
00:15:03,069 --> 00:15:05,405
OKAY.

382
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:07,699
OH, JOEY, COME OVER LATER
'CAUSE I'M GOING TO TEACH YOU

383
00:15:07,699 --> 00:15:09,826
HOW TO MAKE A BIRD FEEDER
OUT OF JUST A PINECONE

384
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:11,244
AND SOME PEANUT BUTTER.

385
00:15:11,244 --> 00:15:13,705
OH... I LOVE BIRDS.

386
00:15:15,373 --> 00:15:17,709
WHAT IS THE MATTER WITH YOU?

387
00:15:17,709 --> 00:15:19,043
WHAT?

388
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:20,127
YOU'RE ARRANGING FLOWERS!

389
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:23,089
YOU GOT DEAD FLOWERS!

390
00:15:23,089 --> 00:15:26,885
YOU GOT TO A PICTURE
OF A BABY DRESSED LIKE FLOWERS!

391
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,096
THIS IS NOT JOEY.

392
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:32,682
HEY, HEY, LOOK, I AM
STILL JOEY, OKAY?

393
00:15:32,682 --> 00:15:34,225
FLOWERS, THEY'RE JUST

394
00:15:34,225 --> 00:15:36,561
YOU KNOW, THEY'RE
NICE TO LOOK AT.

395
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:38,979
AND THAT HAPPENS TO BE A
PICTURE BY A FAMOUS ARTIST

396
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:42,108
OF A FAMOUS BABY.

397
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:44,569
YOU'RE TURNING INTO A WOMAN.

398
00:15:44,569 --> 00:15:46,279
NO, I'M NOT.

399
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:47,405
WHY WOULD YOU SAY THAT?

400
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:49,198
THAT'S JUST MEAN.

401
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:52,577
NOW I'VE UPSET YOU?

402
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:53,661
WHAT DID I SAY?

403
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:54,954
IT'S NOT WHAT YOU SAID

404
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,957
IT'S JUST THE
WAY YOU SAID IT.

405
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,292
OH, MY GOD!

406
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:01,335
I'M A WOMAN!

407
00:16:07,425 --> 00:16:09,928
SO NOW SHE THINKS
THAT I MADE OUT WITH HIM

408
00:16:09,928 --> 00:16:11,846
AND THAT I DID IT TO GET
HER JOB.

409
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:12,847
WELL, WHY DIDN'T YOU
JUST TELL HER THE TRUTH?

410
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:14,515
I DID.

411
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:16,643
BUT SHE DOESN'T THINK THAT
ANYONE WOULD BE STUPID ENOUGH

412
00:16:16,643 --> 00:16:21,105
TO CONFUSE KENNY THE COPY GUY
WITH RALPH LAUREN.

413
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:23,691
WELL, HEY, WHAT IF KENNY
WERE THE REAL BRAINS

414
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:25,192
BEHIND THE WHOLE
COMPANY, YOU KNOW?

415
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:27,528
WHAT IF KENNY HIRED
THAT RALPH LAUREN GUY

416
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:29,029
TO BE THE PRETTY
FRONT MAN, HUH?

417
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:31,658
DID SHE EVER THINK OF THAT?

418
00:16:34,953 --> 00:16:36,871
YOU WERE WITH KENNY TODAY,
WEREN'T YOU?

419
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:39,415
JUST FOR A SECOND.

420
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:41,709
OH... PHOEBE, WHAT AM
I GOING TO DO?

421
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:44,170
WELL, THE ONLY
THING YOU CAN DO.

422
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:45,463
SLEEP WITH RALPH LAUREN.

423
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:50,176
I'M NOT GOING TO SLEEP
WITH RALPH LAUREN.

424
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:52,470
I MEAN, I COULD,
BUT I WOULDN'T.

425
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,597
OH, SLEEP WITH KENNY.

426
00:16:58,476 --> 00:16:59,811
THAT WOULDN'T HELP ME.

427
00:16:59,811 --> 00:17:02,104
OH, YES, IT WOULD.

428
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:07,318
I'VE HAD A REALLY
GOOD TIME TONIGHT.
MMM.

429
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:09,028
YOU KNOW, I RARELY
CONNECT WITH SOMEONE

430
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:10,571
THIS MUCH ON
THE FIRST DATE.

431
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:12,740
HMM-MM, HMM-MM.

432
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,367
ME, NEITHER.

433
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:20,164
I'VE HAD A REALLY GOOD
TIME, TOO, YOU KNOW.

434
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:23,041
ARE YOU GOING TO
EAT THAT BREAD?

435
00:17:23,041 --> 00:17:26,963
OH, I-I-I
JUST LIKE THE SMELL.

436
00:17:26,963 --> 00:17:29,966
( sniffs )...MMM.

437
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:31,258
YOU MAKE ME LAUGH.

438
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:33,302
HM-MMM.

439
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,889
WOULD YOU LIKE TO MOVE
OVER TO THE COUCH?

440
00:17:35,889 --> 00:17:38,892
MM-HMM.

441
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:44,438
MAYBE I'LL JUST TURN
DOWN THE LIGHTS A LITTLE.

442
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:47,525
HOW ABOUT ALL THE WAY?

443
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:49,903
OKAY.

444
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:57,535
WOW, COOL POSTER.

445
00:17:57,535 --> 00:18:01,039
OR, SHOULD I SAY GROOVY POSTER?

446
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:06,419
SO, UH, WHERE WERE WE?

447
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:14,092
ARE THOSE YOUR TEETH?

448
00:18:14,092 --> 00:18:19,766
OH, YOU CAN SEE THEM, HUH?

449
00:18:19,766 --> 00:18:21,809
YES.
THEY'RE INSANELY WHITE.

450
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:26,814
YEAH, I DID THAT FOR YOU.

451
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:29,275
WHAT'S THE MATTER
WITH YOU?

452
00:18:29,275 --> 00:18:30,317
WHAT'S THE MATTER WITH ME?

453
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:31,444
YOU'VE GOT A BLACK LIGHT!

454
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:34,196
IT'S 1999!

455
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:42,747
OH, GOOD.

456
00:18:42,747 --> 00:18:43,748
KIM, HI.

457
00:18:43,748 --> 00:18:45,124
HI, RACHEL.

458
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,793
OH, I'VE BEEN
MEANING TO ASK YOU.

459
00:18:46,793 --> 00:18:48,920
HAVE YOU SEEN THE NEW
RALPH LAUREN SHEETS?

460
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:52,381
WHAT AM I THINKING?
OF COURSE YOU HAVE.

461
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,800
OKAY-- OKAY, LOOK.

462
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:56,385
I'M SORRY
THAT I LIED TO YOU BEFORE.

463
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:57,929
YOU WERE RIGHT.

464
00:18:57,929 --> 00:19:01,348
RALPH AND I WERE AN ITEM,
BUT WE'RE NOT ANYMORE.

465
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:02,683
OH, REALLY?

466
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:05,519
YEAH.
HE DUMPED ME.

467
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:10,024
HE SAID,
"RACHEL, I CAN'T DO THIS.

468
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:12,192
"EVEN THOUGH YOU'RE A VERY,

469
00:19:12,192 --> 00:19:16,447
"VERY, VERY BEAUTIFUL WOMAN

470
00:19:16,447 --> 00:19:17,782
"I CAN'T DO THIS.

471
00:19:17,782 --> 00:19:19,117
I'M MARRIED AND I'M SORRY."

472
00:19:19,117 --> 00:19:20,952
AND THEN--
I DON'T KNOW WHY--

473
00:19:20,952 --> 00:19:23,329
BUT HE SAID, "AND YOU
WILL NEVER GET PROMOTED

474
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:27,000
"ESPECIALLY NOT ABOVE KIM,
WHO IS AN INTEGRAL COG

475
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,418
IN THE RALPH LAUREN MACHINE."

476
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:34,298
YOU EXPECT ME
TO BELIEVE THAT...

477
00:19:34,298 --> 00:19:35,925
HI, RALPH.

478
00:19:35,925 --> 00:19:37,217
HI, KIM.

479
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,446
OH, MY GOD.

480
00:19:57,446 --> 00:20:01,034
HE JUST GAVE YOU THE COLDEST
LOOK I HAVE EVER SEEN.

481
00:20:01,034 --> 00:20:03,369
IT'S LIKE HE HATES YOU.

482
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:04,829
THEN IT IS TRUE?

483
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,166
OF COURSE IT'S TRUE.

484
00:20:08,166 --> 00:20:11,418
AND IT HURTS SO BAD.

485
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:15,840
OH, HONEY, COME HERE.
OH, IT'LL BE OKAY.

486
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:19,301
IT'S JUST WE'VE
ALL BEEN THERE.

487
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:25,599
Y-Y-Y-YOU AND RALPH?

488
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:27,685
KENNY THE COPY BOY.

489
00:20:38,029 --> 00:20:39,030
HEY!

490
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:40,239
HEY, UH...

491
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:41,908
I NEED TO TALK TO YOU.

492
00:20:41,908 --> 00:20:43,034
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

493
00:20:43,034 --> 00:20:44,118
ARE YOU UPSET?

494
00:20:44,118 --> 00:20:45,369
I'M SORRY, BUT WE GOT TO GET RID

495
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:46,871
OF ALL THIS GIRLIE STUFF
IN HERE.

496
00:20:46,871 --> 00:20:48,873
I, UH, I GOT TO BE A MAN.

497
00:20:48,873 --> 00:20:50,541
OKAY?

498
00:20:50,541 --> 00:20:53,335
THE LIVING ROOM HAS TO REMAIN
A GUY PLACE, OKAY?

499
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:55,213
THAT'S JUST THE WAY
IT HAS TO BE.

500
00:20:55,213 --> 00:20:58,049
WELL, IF THAT'S WHAT YOU WANT,
I'LL JUST PUT IT ALL IN MY ROOM.

501
00:20:58,049 --> 00:20:59,383
GOOD.
GREAT... GREAT.

502
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:02,887
AND, UH, THANKS
FOR BEING SO UNDERSTANDING.

503
00:21:02,887 --> 00:21:05,514
I MEAN, I DIDN'T WANT
TO MAKE A BIG DEAL
OUT OF THIS, YOU KNOW.

504
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:08,475
WELL, BUT YOU COULD, UH,
PUT THE PICTURE

505
00:21:08,475 --> 00:21:10,644
OF THE FAMOUS BABY
IN MY ROOM.

506
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:12,354
I MEAN, IF YOU WANT TO.

507
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:15,691
OKAY.

508
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:18,861
AND, UH, MAYBE
THE WATERING CAN THERE.

509
00:21:18,861 --> 00:21:20,362
SURE.

510
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:24,867
AND A COUPLE OF THESE
LITTLE TINY BOXES.

511
00:21:24,867 --> 00:21:27,161
JOEY, DO YOU WANT ME TO
PUT IT ALL IN YOUR ROOM?

512
00:21:27,161 --> 00:21:28,246
OKAY.

